(7132849, 1090971, 18367, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by docpjv:</b></div><hr/><i> I saw this on Facebook and are still having a problem with advertising in other media, be it to 1 or 100 ''friends''. <br/>Wish we could discuss this in open forum. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Perhaps I am misinformed, but I was under the impression that only "friends" could see the image and if such is the case, I doubt that <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=6519" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Beetle</a>has identified many individuals as her friends in Facebook.<br/> <br/>Assuming that the numbers are minimal, what possible impact could this have.  I voted on this image and if you promise not to reveal my score to her I will gladly tell you what it was.  :O)<br/> <br/>Ray</td>', 'Originally posted by docpjv: I saw this on Facebook and are still having a problem with advertising in other media, be it to 1 or 100 ''friends''. Wish we could discuss this in open forum.   Perhaps I am misinformed, but I was under the impression that only "friends" could see the image and if such is the case, I doubt that  Beetlehas identified many individuals as her friends in Facebook. Assuming that the numbers are minimal, what possible impact could this have.  I voted on this image and if you promise not to reveal my score to her I will gladly tell you what it was.  :O) Ray', '2013-11-20 19:15:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7132866, 1090953, 80096, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by spiritualspatula:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a perfect candidate for HDR. Your setting sun has quite obviously overwhelmed your sensor, so doing a combination of exposures to maintain  that would be perfect here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Shooting moving water in HDR (bracketing 5-7 shots) would be difficult, even wind-blown trees look strange when shooting HDRs. The only way to possibly do this would be to create a single image HDR in Photomatix and hope for a good outcome.</td>', 'Originally posted by spiritualspatula: This is a perfect candidate for HDR. Your setting sun has quite obviously overwhelmed your sensor, so doing a combination of exposures to maintain  that would be perfect here.   Shooting moving water in HDR (bracketing 5-7 shots) would be difficult, even wind-blown trees look strange when shooting HDRs. The only way to possibly do this would be to create a single image HDR in Photomatix and hope for a good outcome.', '2013-11-20 20:09:09.000000', NULL, 0),
